{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014701-questions-about-an-upcoming-scene","id":1014701,"title":"Questions about an Upcoming Scene","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-09T04:39:34-08:00","id":1014701,"title":"Questions about an Upcoming Scene","content":"So my pack is running into a burning building (some in Umbra and some in material world) to rescue innocents. There is a group of Fomori trying to kill the innocents and a whole lot of firefighters and police outside. In the Umbra there are fire elementals having a heyday around the building. That is where we ended the session.<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Can the werewolves &quot;physically&quot; hurt the fire elementals with teeth and claw? I would think they would just go right through but in the Umbra they are both spirit essence.<br /> <br /> 3) If the players decide not to fight the fire elementals, what would be a good way to appease them?<br /> <br /> 2) Can the werewolves attack fomori banes in the Umbra or are they too ingrained into the fomori? If they kill the banes in the Umbra, what happens to the fomori in the physical world?<br /> <br /> Thanks all for any help.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2788-armos-black","name":"Armos Black","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:37:14-08:00","id":1014729,"title":"","content":"Once in umbra they are both spirits and they can harm them directly. There should be a section on Umbral Combat. Though attacking Gaian spirits probably won't end well for the Garou when it comes time to gain renown. You might be better off having them be balefire elemental or corrupted fire elemental. Maybe have 1 balefire elemental that has started sorrupting 2 or 3 fire elementals.<br /> <br /> Have a requirement that they need to defeat the Balefire Elemental before they can perform the rite of cleansing to purify the spirits which results in them becoming passive (or at least as passive as a fire elemental can be). <br /> <br /> Mortals can be tormented by banes who are still in the umbra without possessing them, you can attack those. Once a Mortal becomes a Fomori their spirit and the bane have become one. You will not see these Banes in the Umbra as they are riding shotgun in the material world now and extracting them almost always ends with the mortal dying if you try to extract the bane. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T08:30:31-08:00","id":1014782,"title":"","content":"The Garou should be able to bribe the fire elementals into burning something else instead (like, say, the Fomori). That would be much more efficient than fighting them and could prove a useful distraction for the Mortal Authorities while they rescue their friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:43:16-08:00","id":1014806,"title":"","content":"I agree, though they might also be able to convince them to burn the fomori by telling them that the corruption within the fomori would be more fun to burn than simple wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:22:54-08:00","id":1014822,"title":"","content":"On one hand, if there is a balefire elemental, it makes the scenario a rush to kill the nasty beast before it turns the other spirits against the Garou, which is neat and tense; on the other hand, if none of the fire spirits serve the Wyrm, it makes the situation a little more complicated, since going full chainsaw-claws on fellow Gaians is something that could have negative repercussions in the future.<br /> <br /> Assuming for a moment that none of the elementals are corrupt, fighting the spirits is an option if there is no alternative... but keep in mind this could be a great opportunity for your theurge to shine.<br /> <br /> Depending how coherent the fire elementals are, the Garou might be able to bargain with them and say that humans will soon be extinguishing the flames- but if the elementals help against the Wyrm minions, the Garou will allow the place to burn down of its own volition. Of course, then the Garou need to figure out how to stall the cops and fire department, but that is all part of the adventure.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the flame spirits are frenzied and/or bloodthirsty, the werewolves could placate them by offering a sacrifice, and ritually burning themselves. In return, they could request that the elementals similarly burn the Fomori. Maybe make it a 1:3 ratio, where if a Garou gives three health levels of aggravated damage to the fire elementals, the Fomori take 9 levels of damage distributed among them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Either one of these might make allies out of the fire spirits, who may be better predisposed towards the pack in the future.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-09-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:23:12-08:00","id":1014850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Armos Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1014701-questions-about-an-upcoming-scene#post1014701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can the werewolves &quot;physically&quot; hurt the fire elementals with teeth and claw? I would think they would just go right through but in the Umbra they are both spirit essence.<br /> <br /> 3) If the players decide not to fight the fire elementals, what would be a good way to appease them?<br /> <br /> 2) Can the werewolves attack fomori banes in the Umbra or are they too ingrained into the fomori? If they kill the banes in the Umbra, what happens to the fomori in the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird that your numbers are out of order <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1) The 2 worlds are separate and without Gifts each part of the pack will have to deal with their own sides. The physical world Garou probably won't be much help with the Elementals.<br /> <br /> 3) Fire Elementals enjoy burning things. Try and redirect them. Keep in mind that the physical fire and the Elementals are separate. They feed off of each other, but they are 2 distinct things. You would have to get the Elementals across the gauntlet to have them attack the fomori physically. This is just a general thing though. The Elementals may have Charms that allow them to do so without help (but this isn't standard).<br /> <br /> 2) Fomori are purely physical creatures. However, once the fomori is killed the Bane should be released into the Umbra. Offhand, I can't remember if it appears weakened off not though. It will most likely run away once there or reform someplace else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:55:23-08:00","id":1015086,"title":"","content":"1) Spirits are always made of &quot;spirit stuff&quot;, aka ephemera. Therefore all spirits are equally &quot;solid&quot; regardless if they are spirits of air, fire, plants, animals, rocks, etc. unless they have a Charm which changes that. Since Garou are creatures of half reality and half spirit, they are equally solid to spirits as well and vice versa. So yes, a Garou can bite a fire elemental spirit with his teeth and do damage, even though Garou biting real fire in the realm just burns his face off.<br /> <br /> 2) When talking about appeasing spirits, you need to first think what the spirits want to do (inspired by mainly thinking how their counterparts in the Realm generally act). Spirits aren't rational as we use the term. They just are. Fire spirits just want to burn things, because that is what fire does - once started it burns everything it can. I'd say the best way to appease them is to get them to burn something else they'd rather do better (say something more in volume/mass or more flammable). Offer to lead the fire spirits to somewhere else, say by leaving a trail of gasoline to something else that appears more &quot;appetizing&quot;. In the Realm, it should just appear that the fire mysteriously changes direction towards something else.<br /> <br /> 3) Once the Bane possess a human and terms them into Fomori, the Bane becomes part of the human and is no longer separate from them. If you appear in the Umbra, you don't see the Bane. It is just like a fetish - the spirit is in the material fetish, not floating around it in the Umbra. If you can kill the Fomori or somehow expel the Bane from the human, then they might appear in the Umbra once expelled. Unfortunately, the way the rules work, it is very rare to drive a Bane out of a possessed human. You have to kill the Fomori and therefore the human host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:27:05-08:00","id":1015698,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone for the ideas. I think i am going to have about 3 fire elementals being controlled by a more powerful balefire one. The characters are starting to discover the Seventh Generation Snatchers who, because of the pack, are trying to cover tracks. Balefire elemental can be summoned by another caste to eliminate the innocents and the fomori snatchers to end the connection to Seneth Gen.<br /> <br /> FYI: Using Rage Across New York kind of updated to today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2788-armos-black","name":"Armos Black","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:44:04-08:00","id":1015704,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to hearing how it turns out, if you don't mind updating after the session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}